---
layout: page
title: paper-read
permalink: /paper-read/
description: A reading shelf of research papers, with English–Vietnamese translations and notes on the arguments behind the results.
nav: true
nav_order: 3
css:
  - /assets/css/paper-read.css
papers:
  - title: SuperMimic
    subtitle: Scaling Humanoid Whole-Body Control with One Differentiable World Model
    description: One shared world model for learning humanoid motion. A close reading of the method, compute comparisons, and scaling results.
    topic: Humanoid control
    year: 2026
    reader: /supermimic_annotated.html
    preview: /assets/img/paper-read/supermimic.jpg
    source: https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.28480
  - title: REPAIR
    subtitle: "Beyond Policy Patches: Distilling RL Specialists into Vision-Language-Action Policies"
    description: From precision-critical RL specialists to a single VLA policy. Notes on value-guided distillation, on-policy refinement, and the experimental evidence.
    topic: Robot manipulation
    year: 2026
    reader: /repair-annotated.html
    preview: /assets/img/paper-read/repair.jpg
    source: https://www.alphaxiv.org/abs/2611.02777
---
<div class="paper-shelf-meta">
  <span>{{ page.papers | size }} annotated papers</span>
  <span>English / Tiếng Việt</span>
</div>

<ul class="paper-gallery" aria-label="Papers to read">
  {% for paper in page.papers %}
    <li class="paper-card">
      <a class="paper-card-preview" href="{{ paper.reader | relative_url }}" aria-label="Read {{ paper.title | escape }} with annotations">
        <img src="{{ paper.preview | relative_url }}" alt="" width="960" height="600" loading="lazy">
        <span class="paper-card-format">Annotated reading · EN / VI</span>
      </a>
      <div class="paper-card-body">
        <div class="paper-card-meta">
          <span>{{ paper.topic }}</span>
          <span>{{ paper.year }}</span>
        </div>
        <h2>
          <a href="{{ paper.reader | relative_url }}">{{ paper.title }}</a>
        </h2>
        <p class="paper-card-subtitle">{{ paper.subtitle }}</p>
        <p class="paper-card-description">{{ paper.description }}</p>
        <div class="paper-card-links">
          <a href="{{ paper.reader | relative_url }}">Read with annotations <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          <a href="{{ paper.source }}"
            >Original paper <span class="sr-only">({{ paper.title }})</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
          >
        </div>
      </div>
    </li>
  {% endfor %}
</ul>
